  "text": "The picture shows the event you chose. Feedback is unavailable, so these words have not been checked against Sol’s account. They will stay labeled as your suggested ending.\n\nWe measure flour, clean water, yeast and a little salt, then mix and knead them. Kneading means pressing and folding the dough until it holds together and feels stretchy.\n\nLive listening feedback is not available in this local demo. Recording and replay stay in this practice window. Nothing is saved to your adventure or sent automatically.\n\nThis saved adventure used the earlier Sol story. Start a new adventure from Pause to play the bakery, roof repair and thank-you visit. This adventure will be archived.\n\nThe boy promised his sister he would keep the bird safe. The wing was already torn before Mara reached for it. The story does not tell us exactly what he was thinking.\n\n“She wrote me a story?” Grandma looked at the page. “I thought she had nothing more she wanted to tell us. I should have asked her. Come and sit where we can read it.”\n\nWelcome back to the garden. We postponed the gathering so Mara could finish her work and join us. I'll read The Torn Wing for her, and Sol will share A Small Repair.\n\nThe leak would have threatened the flour while I worked. Keeping it dry lets me make the bread I promised. A small repair can make a big difference to someone else.\n\nWelcome back to the garden. We postponed the gathering so Mara could finish her work and join us. Mara will tell The Torn Wing, and Sol will share A Small Repair.\n\nFixing the tile kept the flour dry. Rina could bake the bread she had promised. Later, she brought Sol a loaf to thank him. You can choose which part to show.",
